In triangle $ABC,$ $D$ lies on $\overline{BC}$ and $F$ lies on $\overline{AB}.$  Let $\overline{AD}$ and $\overline{CF}$ intersect at $P.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.8 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, F, P;

A = (1,4);
B = (0,0);
C = (6,0);
D = interp(B,C,7/12);
F = interp(A,B,5/14);
P = extension(A,D,C,F);

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--D);
draw(C--F);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, S);
label("$F$", F, W);
label("$P$", P, SW);
[/asy]

